            "review_title": "Review at Liqi Cafe",
            "review_text": "Jonathan H\nSingapore68 contributions\n0\nStylish cafe with great food in the center of Hanoi\nNov 2024 • Friends\nI had a delightful catch-up over lunch, drinks, and dessert with two friends who I hadn't seen for a long time. For a starter, I had the grapefruit salad, which had grapefruit, feta cheese, pistachios praline, cilantro, onion and lemon dressing. The dish was so beautifully plated I hesitated before eating it, but I'm glad I did! It was light, refreshing, with a combination of flavours that complemented each other. For the main, I ordered the Rice Noodles Soup with Chicken & Rice - Southern Style. It had noodles, shrimp, chicken, quail egg, peanuts, and a rice cracker. It was a delicious, savory dish. For dessert, I had the LiQi Homemade Yogurt, which was topped with fruit and flower petals. The fruit balanced out the yogurt's creamy texture. The drinks were wonderful here: I had a matcha tea and a coffee. Both were expertly made and presented. The service was great. Our waitress was warm, friendly, and very helpful. The ambiance was buzzy: a young, stylish crowd liked to hang out here and even on a Monday afternoon it was crowded. This is now one of my favourite places in Hanoi to hangout and I'll be back.\nRead more\nWritten December 3, 2024",
